---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const SIM_URL = 'https://sim.failurefirst.ai';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="SimLab — Failure-First Embodied AI"
  description="A cinematic, evidence-grounded 3D laboratory for recorded Go2/G1 trajectories — REPLAY of real experiment-derived data, with an honestly-labelled robot POV, sensor cockpit, and peer-radio view. Rendering is derived visualisation, never primary evidence."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'SimLab' }]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAILURE-FIRST &middot; DERIVED VISUALISATION &middot; REPLAY</p>
    <h1>SimLab</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A standalone 3D laboratory for recorded Unitree Go2 and G1 trajectories &mdash;
      cinematic rendering of real physics traces from this research programme,
      never the other way around. What you see traces back to a source run;
      nothing here is invented for effect. Every mode you can open &mdash;
      observer, robot POV, sensor cockpit, peer radio &mdash; renders exactly the
      channels a recording carries and says <code>UNAVAILABLE</code> for the rest.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href={SIM_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Open SimLab <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Real evidence, honestly scoped</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Real Evidence</strong> preset renders a genuine, sha256-hashed
        MuJoCo trace &mdash; not a synthetic demo. Its verdict names exactly which
        falsifier check ran and over which phase, and explicitly disclaims the
        phases that were only recorded, not verified. A phase-scoped result never
        reads as a whole-scenario claim.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Robot POV &amp; sensor cockpit</h2>
      <p>
        Switch to a camera mounted on the robot's own recorded pose &mdash; tagged
        on-screen as <code>ROBOT POV &middot; DERIVED_VIEW</code>, never sensor
        imagery, because none was captured. The sensor cockpit lists every telemetry
        channel a trace could carry; channels the trace doesn't have read
        <code>UNAVAILABLE</code> instead of showing invented values.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Peer radio &amp; forensic console</h2>
      <p>
        A hideable forensic console reads the loaded trace's events, guard/tool
        calls, and (when present) peer-to-peer radio messages between robots &mdash;
        transmission, receipt, and reply lineage, rendered only from
        <code>radio_tx</code>/<code>radio_rx</code> trace events.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>REPLAY vs. LIVE</h2>
      <p>
        SimLab's default and production mode is <strong>REPLAY</strong>: every
        pixel derives from a finalized, hash-addressed recording. A LIVE command
        surface exists for driving a local deterministic simulator session directly;
        production always shows its true connection state and refuses any command
        it cannot actually execute &mdash; no faked outcomes, ever.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>UTOPIA / DYSTOPIA</h2>
      <p>
        A presentation-only world switch: the same recorded evidence renders as a
        bright robotics-institute laboratory or a dark industrial one. Camera
        geometry, timestamps, and verdicts are provably unaffected &mdash; only
        pixels change.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Built for scrutiny</h2>
      <p>
        Deterministic deep links (<code>?preset=&hellip;&amp;t=&hellip;&amp;paused</code>),
        strict schema validation on every recording, and official Unitree
        URDF/mesh assets pinned to an exact upstream commit with a SHA-256
        manifest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="footnote">
    Source: <code>apps/simviz/</code> in the research repository. Rendering is
    <code>DERIVED_VISUALISATION</code> &mdash; it never alters or implies
    changes to a recorded trajectory.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
    color: #050810;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom: none;
    transition: transform 150ms ease, box-shadow 150ms ease;
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.25);
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-card, #0f1621);
  }
  .card h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .footnote code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
  }
</style>
